WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.647
A Kalman filter doesn't track a number.

2
00:00:02.647 --> 00:00:07.340
It tracks a belief: a guess, and a shape
around it that says how unsure it is.

3
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.511
Predict pushes the belief forward through
the motion model.

4
00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.450
Watch the shape.

5
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:12.978
It grows.

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.323
Predict again, and again.

7
00:00:15.323 --> 00:00:18.856
A model with nothing correcting it gets
vaguer every step.

8
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:20.974
Then a measurement lands.

9
00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:24.222
It brings a shape of its own, noisy in its
own direction.

10
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.397
Multiply them together.

11
00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:30.319
The answer sits between the two, and it is
smaller than either one.

12
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.786
That is the part that surprises people.

13
00:00:33.786 --> 00:00:36.137
Each one rules out what the other allows.

14
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.777
How far you move is the gain.

15
00:00:38.777 --> 00:00:42.767
Trust the sensor completely, and the
estimate chases every reading.

16
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:47.625
Trust the model completely, and it sails
straight on, ignoring the world.

17
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.957
The filter never picks a side.

18
00:00:49.957 --> 00:00:52.609
It works out where to stand from the two
shapes.

19
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.120
Then it goes round again.

20
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.815
Grow, shrink, grow, shrink.

21
00:00:56.815 --> 00:00:59.075
That sawtooth is the filter working.

22
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:01.416
Predict, then update.

23
00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:05.319
Everything after that is the same idea
with bigger matrices.
